{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nSix artifacts exist only because a cutover once needed a bar to clear. `src/rebar/llm/review_kernel/discovery_shadow.py` (389 LOC, \"RP-06 S7 — the cross-gate discovery SHADOW comparator\") has zero src importers; its only consumer is `tests/unit/test_review_discovery_shadow.py`. `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/fidelity_spot_eval.py` (492 LOC, epic-c81c spot evals) has no CLI, Make, or CI dispatch, so `main()` at `:407` is unreachable; its two pure helpers `_verdict_decision` `:79` and `_majority_decision` `:127` are imported by `src/rebar/llm/evals/provider_parity.py:52-57` and must be relocated. `src/rebar/llm/code_review/workflow_ops.py:774 shadow_compare` is called only from tests. `src/rebar/llm/workflow/gate_dispatch.py:38-41` re-exports `_attach_code_review_metrics` (canonical home `finalize.py:171`) solely for `tests/unit/test_code_review_fp_ledger.py`. `src/rebar/llm/workflow/lint_refs.py:35,730` passes through `ENGINE_INJECTED_INPUTS` (canonical home `lint_expr.py:41`); the other three names there are used and stay. ADR 0111 `:38-56` forbids internal-only shims. `tests/unit/workflow/test_legacy_helper_retirement_09f6.py` is a string-absence tombstone; ADR 0111 `:108-112` and ADR 0116 `:15,40` reject tombstoning, so it goes. `src/rebar/llm/parity.py` STAYS (`provider_parity.py:45,48` import it); only its `:1` docstring naming LangGraph is residue.\n\n**Every citation was re-measured on origin/main 339c0b3af7b, and each deleted symbol's references were enumerated tree-wide, not sampled.** That sweep corrected two counts: there are **12** `gate_dispatch._attach_code_review_metrics` call sites, not 11, and `shadow_compare` is called from **two** tests, not three scattered lines.\n\n## Approach\n1. `git rm src/rebar/llm/review_kernel/discovery_shadow.py tests/unit/test_review_discovery_shadow.py`. In `docs/review-kernel.md` delete the `APPROVED_DELTAS` sentence ending `:200` and the \"**The shadow comparator**\" paragraph `:202`; the heading `:182`, sensitive-data paragraph `:211` and cache note `:223` also describe the discovery journal, so reword rather than delete.\n2. Move `_verdict_decision`/`_majority_decision` into `parity.py` as public `verdict_decision`/`majority_decision` (the names `provider_parity.py:53,56` already alias them to). Replace `provider_parity.py:48-57` with `from rebar.llm.parity import ItemRecord, majority_decision, verdict_decision` — absorbing the `ItemRecord` import `:48`, blank `:49`, the justifying comment `:50-51`, and both aliased blocks `:52-57`. Lines `:44-47` untouched. **Also rewrite the module docstring `:9` and `:11`**, which name `fidelity_spot_eval` and both underscore helpers; leaving them fails AC1. Then `git rm src/rebar/llm/plan_review/fidelity_spot_eval.py src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/fidelity_spot_eval_results.json tests/unit/test_fidelity_spot_eval.py`. Rewrite `parity.py:1-4` to describe the non-inferiority bar `provider_parity` scores against. Edit `container_stage.py:80`, `docs/config.md:413` (drop the `main()` allowlist clause), `eval_specs/README.plan-review.md:86,101-102`.\n3. Delete both `shadow_compare` tests from `tests/unit/test_code_review_discovery.py` — `:246-255` and `:258-268`, plus separating blanks `:256-257`, `:269-270`. The AC2 comment `:271` and test `:272` are unrelated and STAY. Then delete `shadow_compare` from `workflow_ops.py:774` to the end of that function.\n4. `gate_dispatch.py`: drop `_attach_code_review_metrics` from the `:38-41` import (keep `CODE_REVIEW_STEP_IDS`, used `:443`), delete the `:36` comment and `:289` marker. In `test_code_review_fp_ledger.py` add `from rebar.llm.code_review.finalize import _attach_code_review_metrics` and rewrite all **12** calls at `:188,204,218,233,252,270,292,328,344,379,395,419`.\n5. `lint_refs.py`: drop `ENGINE_INJECTED_INPUTS` from the `:35` import and `__all__` `:730`. `lint.py:27` keeps the rest from `.lint_refs` and takes that name from `.lint_expr` (`:128` consumes it unchanged). `tests/unit/workflow/test_contracts.py:18` retargets to `lint_expr`. Rewrite the `lint_expr.py:12` back-compat re-export clause.\n6. `git rm tests/unit/workflow/test_legacy_helper_retirement_09f6.py`.\n7. `docs/research/task-decomposition-sota-2026.md:167` cites `fidelity_spot_eval` as a live batch-rerun seam. Reword to name only `production_batch_runner`; AC1 cannot pass otherwise.\n8. `tests/unit/test_provider_parity.py:150` is a comment naming `_verdict_decision`. Retarget it to the public `verdict_decision`. Non-breaking, but it would otherwise be a stale private-name reference to a deleted symbol.\n\n## Scope\nThe artifacts above plus their exclusive tests and docs. **Cleared by the tree-wide sweep, no edit needed:** `tests/unit/test_review_bot_token_metrics.py:19`, `tests/unit/test_code_review_finalize.py:15`, `src/rebar/llm/code_review/batch_runner.py:157` all reference the CANONICAL `finalize._attach_code_review_metrics`, which stays. Also out: `parity.py` (live), `code_review/shim.py`, `evals/plan_replay/legacy_v4_baseline.py`, `tests/unit/test_gate_engine_cutover.py`, and `provider_parity.py:88 AGENTIC_SOLVERS` (eval-harness epic; this story touches only `:9,:11,:48-57` there, and the file-impact overlap serialises the two through next-batch).\n\n## Testing\n`git rm tests/unit/test_plan_review_prerequisites_continuation_heldout.py` **entirely**: its `:8` module import is shared by all 4 tests and three call into the deleted module (`:38`, `:61`, `:69`, `:120`). Deleting one test would leave an unimportable module.\n`tests/unit/test_container_roster.py`: drop `fidelity_spot_eval` from the `:13` import and the roster tuples `:97`, `:102`; `pass1` and `eval_solver` remain.\n`tests/unit/test_subcall_class_selection.py`: delete the `_relocation_requests` entry `:247` and rows `:495-496`.\n`tests/unit/test_rp01_s5_authoritative_oracle.py`: replace the `:182` assertion `assert \"fidelity_spot_eval.py\" in files` with the synthetic `assert _scope_constructs_structured(ast.parse('def f(p):\\n    mode = \"structured\" if p else \"findings\"\\n    RunRequest(mode=mode)\\n'), {})`, keeping the `jira_dc_capability_map.py` assertion. **It cannot be repointed at another real file: `fidelity_spot_eval.py:101` is the tree's ONLY computed-mode consumer**, which is precisely what that assertion guards. **Measured impact on the `:189` floor guard `assert len(files) >= 10`:** the census is **11** today (`completion_subcall, epic_bug_screen, eval_solver, fidelity_spot_eval, jira_dc_capability_map, passes, prerequisites, tier1, tier2, workflow_ops, xcheck`); removing one leaves **10**, so the guard still passes — but its margin becomes zero. Keep the floor at 10 rather than lowering it: it remains a valid \"narrowed or zero-match census\" guard, and lowering it would weaken the only thing protecting that census.\n`tests/unit/test_parity_bar.py:248`: retarget the docstring reference; add `test_verdict_decision_and_majority_decision` (FAIL gives block, findings give block, PASS gives advisory, tie gives block).\n`.github/complexity-baseline.json` is unaffected; deleted symbols bucket `stale`.\nRe-run the tree-wide per-symbol sweep before trusting the greps below; this plan's two count errors were both found that way.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `git grep -n \"discovery_shadow\\|fidelity_spot_eval\\|shadow_compare\\|_attach_code_review_metrics\" -- src docs` returns only `src/rebar/llm/code_review/finalize.py` hits.\n- [ ] `git grep -n \"ENGINE_INJECTED_INPUTS\" -- src tests` shows no hit in `lint_refs.py`.\n- [ ] Every surviving `ENGINE_INJECTED_INPUTS` importer resolves to `lint_expr`.\n- [ ] `python -c \"from rebar.llm.evals import provider_parity; print(provider_parity.verdict_decision({'verdict':'FAIL'}))\"` prints `block`.\n- [ ] `git ls-files tests/unit/workflow/test_legacy_helper_retirement_09f6.py tests/unit/test_review_discovery_shadow.py tests/unit/test_fidelity_spot_eval.py tests/unit/test_plan_review_prerequisites_continuation_heldout.py` prints nothing.\n- [ ] `git grep -c \"gate_dispatch._attach_code_review_metrics\" -- tests` prints nothing.\n- [ ] `tests/unit/test_code_review_fp_ledger.py` passes.\n- [ ] `tests/unit/test_rp01_s5_authoritative_oracle.py` passes, with `len(_structured_consumer_files()) == 10`.\n- [ ] `make verify` exits 0.\n- [ ] `python scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py --check` reports `new=0`."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1793169786510238272,"uuid":"fd5182a4-63f2-48ac-984f-2ccb94487d56"}